    title: "Your Perfect Day in Tifton",
    dek: "Small-town Southern charm, local flavor, and the Friendliest City there ever was.",
    heroImage: "/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/01-brunch-cheers.jpg",
    gallery: ["/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/02-karen-at-berry-good-on-swing.jpg","/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/03-mural-with-the-webbs.jpg","/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/04-rtb-crowd-from-stage.jpg","/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/05-6f07c0a8-5ae6-498f-b128-41a4520a4351.jpg","/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/06-downtown-shoppers-crossing-street.jpg","/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/07-25313106-efa4-461a-93e5-1438c0ac96e1.jpg","/destinations/summer-2026/visit-tifton/08-e41-with-halls.jpg"],
    paragraphs: [
      "YOUR PERFECT DAY IN TIFTON: SMALL TOWN CHARM, BIG SOUTHERN FLAVOR Looking for the perfect Southern getaway? Whether you’re just passing through or planning a day of discovery, Tifton has everything you need—from fresh coffee and local eats to historic charm and outdoor fun. Here’s your go-to guide for spending a full, flavorful day in the Friendliest City there ever was. Start Your Day RightBegin your morning at Mi-Lady Bakery, a local treasure since 1959.",
      "With fresh-brewed coffee and handmade-from-scratch sweet treats lining the cases, it’s the kind of breakfast that feels like home, baked with love. And there is no doubt you will get a “Good Morning” from the locals when you visit. Shop Small, Shop LocalSwing by Savor the Flavor, where Georgia-made goodies take center stage. Sip on a wine slushie while browsing snacks, sauces, and handmade gifts.",
      "Then pop into Plantation 59, The Pineapple Post, Tilly Hill, and The Little Lane Shop for stylish finds, home decor, or a little treat for yourself. Antique hunters? Don’t miss 3rd & Main, Bula’s Antiques, Fifth Street Interiors, and Southern Pickers. These shops are packed with charm and rare finds. Midday Munchies? Go LocoLunchtime calls for flavor, and Taco Loco always delivers. Known for bold tacos, fresh salads, and irresistible street corn, this local hotspot is the perfect pick-me-up.",
      "Pull up a chair and dig in; you’ll be glad you did. Play the South Georgia WayStretch your legs at Fulwood Park, featuring a paved walking trail, 18-hole disc golf course, two playgrounds, dog parks for pups of all sizes, and shaded picnic spots. The park also hosts major events like Rhythm & Ribs BBQ Festival, La Fiesta del Pueblo, and Arts in Black throughout the year. Walk Through HistoryStep back in time at ABAC’s Georgia Museum of Agriculture.",
      "Ride the steam engine train, tour the 19th-century village, and discover how agriculture shaped this region’s story. Through a variety of programs and hands-on experiences, guests connect to where their food, fiber, and shelter come from! It’s a must-see for families, history lovers, and curious minds. Pick TiftonEnd your afternoon with a stop at Berry Good Farms or Rutland Farms. Both offer seasonal u-pick produce, homemade ice cream, fresh lemonade, baked goods, and farm stores full of Georgia Grown favorites.",
      "You may even find a few animals to love on while you’re there. Fuel Up for the RoadBefore heading out, make a stop at Espresso 41. Right off I-75, this funky coffee shop serves up more than just caffeine—from handcrafted lattes to juicy burgers, every bite and sip is made with love and local pride. Plus, it features a great Tifton photo opportunity. Make It a Day to RememberTifton’s heart beats with hometown pride, flavorful food, and friendly faces.",
      "Whether you’re here for a quick visit or a full day of exploring, there’s always something worth savoring.",
      "Stay the Night If you aren’t quite ready to leave yet, we’ve got accommodations to suit your budget and your needs. From mid-tier to award-winning higher-tier hotels, we’ve got it. If a home is more your style, we’ve got Airbnbs in town and out of town. Brought the family in the camper? No problem! We would love for you to stay a while.",
    ],
