      "In St. Pete–Clearwater, luxury and local live side by side. Sugar-white sand beaches by day, MICHELIN‑recommended plates by night. Golden hour hits Beach Drive, and you slow down without meaning to. Palms cast long shadows across the sand; The Vinoy Hotel and Resort blushes pink; and the air smells salty with a hint of butter and citrus, surely coming from a table nearby. Your reservation is a short walk away, so you take the long way along the water. This is what will surprise you about St.",
      "Pete-Clearwater: You don't have to choose between the beach and everything else you want from a vacation. You can have a lazy beach day and then have dinner that looks like a magazine spread at MICHELIN-recommended Il Ritorno, where Italy meets the Gulf on a plate. , dip in and out of local shops like Book + Bottle, then end with craft cocktails at Dirty Laundry, a hidden speakeasy disguised as a laundromat. Walkability is a luxury here, and spontaneity is the point.",
      "The beaches are just as close and feel just as easy. In the morning, cross to St. Pete Beach, cruise north along Gulf Blvd. to Upham Beach for beach time with a book and a Cuban from Bodega at the Secret Garden. Another day, check out Clearwater Beach on Mandalay Ave. and tackle a grouper sandwich you’ll need both hands to enjoy. Nights fall warm and fast. Rooftop toast or a pier stroll to catch the sunset show? You can’t go wrong.",
