      "At Fortu, MICHELIN-recommended omakase unfolds at the chef's counter with grilled Wagyu and creative cocktails that keep pace with each course. The beach is often why you come, but everything else keeps you going. The Warehouse Arts District on 7th Ave. S pulls you into galleries and studios tucked inside The Factory. Drive north to Dunedin's brick Main Street for a pint and epic sunset views at Hi-Fi Rooftop Bar, then hop the Caladesi ferry from nearby Honeymoon Island for an hour of empty beach. a.",
